# The LLVM release Hew builds against. This file is the one place the LLVM
# version is written down; CI (.github/actions/llvm-version and setup-llvm),
# the Makefile and the release scripts read it. `make llvm-version-check`
# verifies that hew-codegen-rs/Cargo.toml (llvm-sys and the inkwell feature)
# and every LLVM_SYS_<ver>_PREFIX reference agree with it.
#
# Plain KEY=value lines only: this file is sourced by sh, included by make and
# appended to $GITHUB_ENV, so no quotes, spaces or expansions.
#
# To bump LLVM:
#   1. Edit LLVM_MAJOR / LLVM_SERIES / LLVM_VERSION below.
#   2. Bump llvm-sys and the inkwell llvmNN-M feature in hew-codegen-rs/Cargo.toml.
#   3. Replace the SHA256 digests below with the subject digests of the
#      sigstore attestations published next to each tarball at
#      https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases/tag/llvmorg-<LLVM_VERSION>
#      (<asset>.jsonl). Never copy a digest from anywhere else.
#   4. Make sure hew-lang/llvm-toolchain has published the
#      toolchain/llvm-<LLVM_SERIES>-windows-msvc release.
#   5. Run `make llvm-version-check`.

# Major version: selects distro packages (llvm@N, llvm-N-dev, FreeBSD llvmN)
# and the llvm-sys crate generation.
LLVM_MAJOR=23
# Release series: selects llvm-sys (major * 10 + minor), the inkwell feature
# and the floating hew-lang/llvm-toolchain Windows release. Any maintenance
# release in this series is supported.
LLVM_SERIES=23.1
# Upstream tarball CI downloads on Linux. Only this release is pinned, and
# only because its digests are pinned below.
LLVM_VERSION=23.1.6
# SHA256 of LLVM-<LLVM_VERSION>-Linux-X64.tar.xz.
LLVM_SHA256_LINUX_X64=bd4d1c434ff69ef06d19e7934c04708da677e5f2eb51f5bcf052ab91818f0094
# SHA256 of LLVM-<LLVM_VERSION>-Linux-ARM64.tar.xz.
LLVM_SHA256_LINUX_ARM64=e9daa167da28b9e31d30046f05f98e3e7da3647cdbe1c1863e8b223c07ccf291
